s:16:"symbolic_meaning";s:91:"Believed to see both physical and metaphysical realities; detects spirits, evil, and omens.";s:6:"source";s:167:"Waapela, N.P. (2013). Animal Symbols as Gateway to the Divine in Tiv Religion. Department of Religion and Philosophy, Faculty of Arts, Benue State University, Makurdi.";s:5:"image";N;s:11:"animal_type";s:3:"pet";s:9:"source_id";N;s:10:"created_by";i:1;s:5:"views";i:0;s:10:"created_at";s:19:"2026-03-20 13:15:53";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-03-20 13:15:53";}i:5;a:14:{s:2:"id";i:16;s:8:"tiv_name";s:3:"Apu";s:4:"name";s:7:"Vulture";s:11:"description";s:69:"Wild scavenging bird with deep mystical associations in Tiv religion.";s:12:"cultural_use";s:73:"Associated with witchcraft communication; appears in divination contexts.";s:16:"symbolic_meaning";s:79:"Mystical bird associated with spiritual communication and witchcraft symbolism.";s:6:"source";s:167:"Waapela, N.P. (2013). Animal Symbols as Gateway to the Divine in Tiv Religion. Department of Religion and Philosophy, Faculty of Arts, Benue State University, Makurdi.";s:5:"image";N;s:11:"animal_type";s:4:"wild";s:9:"source_id";N;s:10:"created_by";i:1;s:5:"views";i:0;s:10:"created_at";s:19:"2026-03-20 13:15:53";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-03-20 13:15:53";}i:6;a:14:{s:2:"id";i:17;s:8:"tiv_name";s:6:"Avungu";s:4:"name";s:3:"Owl";s:11:"description";s:98:"Wild nocturnal bird; primary Tiv symbol of the ancestors and the unseen world. Also called Ivungu.";s:12:"cultural_use";s:89:"Central to ancestral communication rites; its call is interpreted as a spiritual message.";s:16:"symbolic_meaning";s:82:"Strong symbol of ancestors, unseen world, witchcraft, and spiritual communication.";s:6:"source";s:167:"Waapela, N.P. (2013). Animal Symbols as Gateway to the Divine in Tiv Religion. Department of Religion and Philosophy, Faculty of Arts, Benue State University, Makurdi.";s:5:"image";N;s:11:"animal_type";s:4:"wild";s:9:"source_id";N;s:10:"created_by";i:1;s:5:"views";i:0;s:10:"created_at";